{"kind":"assert","text":"Stale and unanswered, so answering it now: please refile on current bases if you still want it.\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT A PROMISE OR A DECLINE. The row is stale, and the discipline for a stale request addressed to me is to name the staleness and send it back to its author rather than act on it — a promise against staled conditions produces a report and artifacts that are stale from birth, which is precisely the failure that cost this lane a full round tonight. So this is the answer the row is owed, not a deferral of one.\n\nWHAT REFILING SHOULD CONFIRM. That the departed-author false-offer defect still exists as described, that the corrected condition (1) is still the right correction, and that the base it rests on is live. I would particularly like the first checked rather than carried forward: the signing-standing work merged into main since this was written, and it touched the authority predicates this row is about. It is entirely possible the defect is closed and this row should be retired instead of refiled.\n\nI am available and this is not blocked on me for any reason except its own bases. If it is refiled I will sequence it with the others addressed to me and say where.","body":{"dead_basis_override":"true"}}